### PATCH 2 â€” Stage 3: Fix DNA extractor same root cause (C1 extension)

**Problem (lines 188â€“209):** State machine uses `$trimmed -match '"role"\s*:\s*"([^"]+)"'` which technically matches the substring â€” but then `$currentBlock += "`n$line"` accumulates **raw JSON lines** as DNA content. So DNA records are JSON blobs not prose. Also: `thinking` content blocks (type `"thinking"`) appear before `"text"` blocks and would be included as garbage.

**Replace the state machine body (the `foreach` loop, lines 188â€“245):**
```powershell
# NEW â€” per-line JSON parse, walk content array for type='text' only
$lines | ForEach-Object {
    $o = $_.Trim() | ConvertFrom-Json -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if (-not $o) { return }
    $role = if ($o.message) { $o.message.role } else { $o.role }
    if ($role -ne 'assistant') { return }
    $content = if ($o.message) { $o.message.content } else { $o.content }
    $text = if ($content -is [string]) { $content }
             elseif ($content -is [array]) { ($content | Where-Object { $_.type -eq 'text' } | ForEach-Object { $_.text }) -join "`n" }
    $text = if ($text) { $text.Trim() } else { "" }
    if ($text.Length -lt 10) { return }
    $turnSeq++
    $isBlueprint = ($text -match '```|\b(SPEC|SPECIFICATION|BLUEPRINT|ARCHITECTURE|SCHEMA|DESIGN)\b' -and $text.Length -gt 200)
    $script:dnaRecords += [ordered]@{ run=$run; seq=$turnSeq; type=if ($isBlueprint) {"blueprint"} else {"prose"}; chars=$text.Length; text=$text }
}
```

Remove the EC-026 dual-hash drift check (it was measuring two broken paths against each other â€” meaningless once both use the same parser). Keep the `$dnaCount`/`$dnaBlueprintCount` derivation and file write.

