## Spaced repetition: engine BUILT, ingestion BROKEN

The SM-2 engine is real and OBI already uses it. But the path you just described â€” **share class audio â†’ add the words â†’ they come back for review** â€” is severed. There are three incompatible KV schemas fighting each other:

| Store | Schema | Written by | Read by |
|-------|--------|-----------|---------|
| `srs_data_<id>` (map: wordâ†’SM-2) | âœ… canonical | OBI auto-capture `/api/agent/vocab` ([index.js:1268](APPS/NET-PET-AI/src/index.js#L1268)) | **OBI due-word injection** ([index.js:1094](APPS/NET-PET-AI/src/index.js#L1094)) |
| `vocab_list_<id>` + `vocab:<id>:<word>` | word list only | `/api/vocab/add` ([index.js:3573](APPS/NET-PET-AI/src/index.js#L3573)) | portal vocab widget |
| `srs:<id>:due` / `srs:<id>:<word>` | orphan | `/api/vocab/review` ([index.js:3610](APPS/NET-PET-AI/src/index.js#L3610)) | `/api/vocab/due` ([index.js:3591](APPS/NET-PET-AI/src/index.js#L3591)) |

**What this means for Mai's class:** `vocab-admin.html` (your tool for adding class words) POSTs to `/api/vocab/add`. That handler writes the word to `vocab_list_` but **never creates an SRS schedule in `srs_data_`**. So every word you add from class audio lands in a dead list â€” OBI never drills it, and the portal's "WORDS DUE" badge reads a third orphan key (`srs:id:due`) that nothing ever writes. The review loop only works for words OBI catches *itself* mid-conversation, not the ones you curate from class.

You're right: now's the time. It's a contained fix â€” three handlers converge onto the `srs_data_` store OBI already trusts.

